{
 "about": "BT2a: how catalogue records and places reach the building types (bidb.type_map). `classes`: Wikidata class labels the FISH thesaurus lacks, or finds too generally, given a type. `within_period`: types whose FISH concept is wider than the type, found through FISH only for records begun within the type's period of use. `nations`: types found only in those nations. `names`: patterns on the name of a record or place none of whose classes finds a type, limited to categories (catalogue) or kinds (places). `categories`: a catalogue category that means one type. `place_kinds`, `place_types`: places by kind, or by their own type label (register types such as 'Castle - tower house'). `not_in_tree`: labels reviewed and left without a type (too general, or no such type in the tree yet), so the report lists only unreviewed ones. `skip_kinds`: place kinds that are not buildings or structures (objects, plaques, finds, events, clubs, firms), never typed.",
